---
// /methodology (Methodology.dc.html): the ledger of imperfections. Every tile
// derives from a stats.json key that exists (methodologyM1Tiles names them and
// tests assert the mapping); M2 renders honest absence when the module is not
// in the build; the publication block carries the REAL build id + manifest sha.
// Mockup numbers with no live source are dropped/reworded — register entries.
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { getBuildData, methodologyM1Tiles } from "../../lib/data";
import { fmtInt } from "../../lib/format";
import { filingWindow } from "../../lib/derive";

const build = getBuildData();
const m1 = methodologyM1Tiles(build.stats, build.filedFrom);
const inst = build.inst;
const window = inst.present ? filingWindow(build.generatedAtDate) : null;

const description =
  "Per-module sources and conditions, coverage measured against the full corpus, known gaps, " +
  "and the structural caveats no engineering removes — regenerated from stats.json on every build.";
---

<Base title="Methodology — Public Filings" description={description} active="methodology">
  <main class="shell page methodology">
    <div class="kicker">/methodology</div>
    <h1 class="metho-title">
      Every number on this site is imperfect in a specific, knowable way. This
      page is the ledger of those imperfections.
    </h1>
    <p class="metho-lede">
      Public Filings republishes primary government records — nothing else. Below, per
      module: sources and their license conditions, coverage measured against
      the full corpus, known gaps, and the structural caveats that no amount of
      engineering removes. Everything here is regenerated from
      <span class="mono-id">stats.json</span> on every build and is
      byte-verifiable against the published snapshot.
    </p>
    <nav class="toc" aria-label="Sections">
      <a href="#m1">M1 · Congressional</a>
      <a href="#m2">M2 · Institutional 13F</a>
      <a href="#m3m4" class="toc-muted">M3 · Financials — planned</a>
      <a href="#m3m4" class="toc-muted">M4 · Macro — planned</a>
      <a href="#publication">Publication &amp; verification</a>
      <a href="#privacy">Privacy</a>
    </nav>

    <section class="metho-section" id="m1">
      <div class="metho-section-head">
        <h2 class="section-h2">M1 — Congressional trading</h2>
        <div class="mono-note">build {build.buildId} · generated {build.generatedAtDate}</div>
      </div>
      <blockquote class="standing-caveat">
        {/* The two facts this caveat carries are linked separately from the
            reader-facing surfaces, so each sentence gets its own stable anchor.
            Text is unchanged — only the wrapping spans and ids are new. */}
        <span id="amount-ranges">Standing caveat: trades are disclosed in statutory dollar ranges, never
        exact amounts</span>, and <span id="filing-lag">may be filed up to 45 days after the trade —
        sometimes later. A filing is a disclosure event, not a market event.</span>
      </blockquote>
      <div class="metho-tiles">
        {m1.map((t) => (
          <div class="mtile">
            <div class={`tile-value${t.muted ? " muted" : ""}`}>{t.value}{t.unit && <span class="unit">{t.unit}</span>}</div>
            <div class="tile-label">{t.label}</div>
            <div class="mtile-sub">{t.sub}</div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div class="metho-grid">
        <div>
          <h3 class="section-h">Sources &amp; conditions</h3>
          <div class="source-list">
            <div class="source-row">
              <div><div class="source-name">House Clerk — PTR disclosures</div><div class="mono-note">us-gov-house · public record</div></div>
              <div class="source-cond">Fetched sequentially with a contact UA. Raw PDFs archived; every rendered row links to its page.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="source-row">
              <div><div class="source-name">Senate eFD</div><div class="mono-note">us-gov-senate · agreement-gated</div></div>
              <div class="source-cond">Accessed only through the eFD prohibition agreement handshake; §13107(c) restrictions carried on every derived surface.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="source-row">
              <div><div class="source-name">congress-legislators</div><div class="mono-note">cc0 · member identity</div></div>
              <div class="source-cond">CC0 seed for bioguide IDs, parties, terms. Joins are conservative: unique-candidate only, publicly versioned aliases.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="source-row">
              <div><div class="source-name">kadoa congress-trading seed</div><div class="mono-note">mit-kadoa-seed · backfill</div></div>
              <div class="source-cond">MIT-licensed historical seed, imported under a blocking human audit gate; retired row-by-row as primary filings supersede it.</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          {/* `/congress/`'s head links `/methodology/#coverage`;
              the id never existed, so the link resolved to the top
              of the page. This is the section it always meant. */}
          <h3 class="section-h" id="coverage">Known gaps — published, not hidden</h3>
          <div class="gaps-block" id="defaults">
            <div>· {fmtInt(build.stats.totals.needs_ocr_filing_count_including_excluded)} paper filings <span class="flag dashed">needs OCR</span> — counted in totals labeled *_including_excluded</div>
            <div>· {fmtInt(build.stats.totals.unresolved_pair_count)} filer name-pairs not yet joined to members — the join is name × chamber × term, only on a unique candidate; the alias file is version-controlled and public</div>
            <div>· amendments carry <span class="flag amber">amendment pending</span> until amendment semantics are settled — the default view (v_default_transactions) excludes the superseded original, and both readings are queryable</div>
            <div>· rows with defect flags are visible and flagged, never dropped</div>
          </div>
          {/* The ONE anchor whose text was not already on this page. Moved
              verbatim from `lib/ui.ts`'s member-page `.entity-lede`, which
              was converted to a note in the same change — the claim relocates, it is not
              duplicated and it is not newly authored. */}
          <h3 class="section-h" id="owner-codes">Whose trade is it — owner codes</h3>
          <div class="gaps-block">
            <div>· Filings under a member include transactions by spouse (SP), dependent
              children (DC), and joint accounts (JT) — the STOCK Act does not distinguish
              who directed a trade.</div>
            <div>· Amounts are statutory ranges; member totals are therefore ranges too.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="metho-section" id="m2">
      <div class="metho-section-head">
        <h2 class="section-h2">M2 — Institutional 13F</h2>
        <div class="mono-note">
          {inst.present
            ? `in this build · latest period ${inst.watermarks.latest_period_of_report ?? "—"} · latest filing ${inst.watermarks.latest_filed_date ?? "—"}`
            : "not in this build"}
        </div>
      </div>
      <blockquote class="standing-caveat" id="13f-scope">
        Standing caveat: 13F covers long positions in Section 13(f) securities —
        no shorts, no cash — as quarter-end snapshots filed up to 45 days late,
        in era-dependent value units. Only managers over $100M file: it is not a
        census.
      </blockquote>
      {inst.present ? (
        <div class="metho-tiles">
          <div class="mtile">
            <div class="tile-value">{fmtInt(inst.filers.length)}</div>
            <div class="tile-label">filers on record</div>
            <div class="mtile-sub">agg_filer_registry</div>
          </div>
          <div class="mtile">
            <div class="tile-value">{inst.watermarks.latest_period_of_report ?? "—"}</div>
            <div class="tile-label">latest period</div>
            <div class="mtile-sub">manifest watermark</div>
          </div>
          <div class="mtile">
            <div class="tile-value">{fmtInt(inst.topn)}</div>
            <div class="tile-label">top-N ranking depth</div>
            <div class="mtile-sub">a Public Filings build parameter</div>
          </div>
          {window?.open && (
            <div class="mtile">
              <div class="tile-value">{window.deadline}</div>
              <div class="tile-label">13F window open until</div>
              <div class="mtile-sub">quarter {window.quarterEnd}</div>
            </div>
          )}
        </div>
      ) : (
        <div class="absent-block">
          <h3 class="absent-h">This build does not include the institutional module.</h3>
          <p>
            When a build publishes the institutional aggregate, its coverage
            stats render here from the module's own manifest watermarks —
            until then this section states absence instead of estimating.
          </p>
        </div>
      )}
      <h3 class="section-h">What our 13F derivations do — and refuse to do</h3>
      <div class="gaps-block cols-2">
        <div>· Amendments are typed: a restatement supersedes; new-holdings merges. Originals are tombstoned, never deleted.</div>
        <div>· A change with an undisclosed side is <strong>n/c</strong> — never coerced into add or trim.</div>
        <div>· "Exit" is a fact about the filing sequence, not a sale: delisting, confidential treatment, and filer migration all look identical in the record.</div>
        <div>· Cross-filer rankings stop at the aggregate's top-N slice, stated in place as a Public Filings build parameter.</div>
        <div>· Concentration is computed only when the denominator is disclosed; otherwise the stat prints "n/a" with its reason <span class="mono-id">concentration_unavailable</span>.</div>
        <div id="13f-identity">· Ticker→issuer joins use the SEC's present-day ticker file against entity-keyed issuers only — never a name match, never a guessed identity.</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="metho-section" id="m3m4">
      <div class="metho-grid">
        <div>
          <h2 class="section-h2">M3 — Company financials <span class="badge-planned">PLANNED</span></h2>
          <p class="metho-planned">
            As-reported XBRL from EDGAR, for a curated universe. Standing caveat,
            committed now: <em>as-reported ≠ normalized comparables</em> —
            restatements and taxonomy drift will be shown as vintages, not
            silently overwritten. This section fills in when the module ships;
            its gates are published before its data.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 class="section-h2">M4 — Macro <span class="badge-planned">PLANNED</span></h2>
          <p class="metho-planned">
            Treasury curve, CPI, employment, COT positioning from agency
            sources. Standing caveat, committed now: <em>series are revised</em>
            — each print carries vintage semantics per series, and BLS-derived
            responses carry the BLS-required citation and disclaimer verbatim.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="metho-section" id="publication">
      <h2 class="section-h2">Publication &amp; verification</h2>
      <div class="pub-grid">
        <div class="pub-card"><div class="pub-h">Immutable snapshots</div><div class="pub-body">Each release is a content-addressed snapshot; the page you are reading names the build it was rendered from.</div></div>
        <div class="pub-card"><div class="pub-h">Signed pointer</div><div class="pub-body">A signed pointer names the current release; per-artifact digests let anyone verify a downloaded extract byte-for-byte.</div></div>
        <div class="pub-card"><div class="pub-h">Reproducible builds</div><div class="pub-body">Same inputs, same bytes. The pipeline, its test suite, and this site's generator are MIT-licensed.</div></div>
        <div class="pub-card"><div class="pub-h">Raw documents retained</div><div class="pub-body">Every parsed filing links to its archived government document; reparses never re-fetch, so the archive is the evidence.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="mono-note verify-line">
        {/* No `--manifest sha256:…` argument: the publish pipeline re-assembles
            the manifest after this site builds, so a digest rendered here would
            be stale by construction and every reader who pasted the command
            would get a mismatch. `--build` alone is sufficient — `populus
            verify` resolves the manifest from the build id. */}
        verify this page: <span class="verify-cmd">populus verify --build {build.buildId}</span>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="metho-section" id="privacy">
      <div class="metho-grid">
        <div>
          <h2 class="section-h2">Privacy — the reader is not the product</h2>
          <p class="metho-body">
            Public Filings measures page traffic with Cloudflare Web
            Analytics, and nothing else. It sets no cookie, writes no storage
            key, and builds no fingerprint or cross-site identifier, and no
            account is required for anything on this site. What the beacon
            records is the page URL without its query string, the referrer, a
            coarse user-agent, a viewport bucket, load timing, and a country
            derived at the server from the connection. Cloudflare retains
            unsampled beacon data for 7 days, then aggregates it to roughly
            10%; the previous six months remain accessible (Cloudflare Web
            Analytics FAQ, retrieved 2026-08-15). Free-text
            search never leaves your device — searches resolve to page paths
            client-side against an index that ships with the build. Watchlists
            live in your browser's localStorage and are never transmitted. If
            Public Filings ever offers paid conveniences (notifications,
            integrations), the records themselves stay free and ungated — a
            transparency site that paywalled the public record would contradict
            this page.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 class="section-h2">Required notices</h2>
          <p class="metho-body">
            <strong>Prohibited uses.</strong> Use of congressional
            financial-disclosure reports for commercial purposes, for
            determining credit, or for solicitation is restricted by 5 U.S.C.
            § 13107(c). <strong>Not financial advice.</strong> Public Filings reports
            disclosures; it recommends nothing. <strong>Attribution.</strong>
            Data remain U.S. government records; per-source conditions are
            recorded in the machine-readable conditions register and rendered in
            <a href="/legal/DATA-LICENSE.md">DATA-LICENSE ↗</a> and
            <a href="/legal/NOTICE.txt">NOTICE ↗</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
